cbs_vp9: check superframe frame sizes without overflowing size_t (CVE-2026-125253)

cbs_vp9_split_fragment() added each frame size from the superframe index to the
position before comparing with the fragment size, so a huge frame size wrapped
and passed the check, and the split read out of bounds.

Backport of FFmpeg master 6280907da48c4dd78f95ef5c713a29c7702153a3 (PR 25232, merged 2026-10-25), not in n9.0.2.
Only the hunk line numbers differ from the master commit.

diff --git a/libavcodec/cbs_vp9.c b/libavcodec/cbs_vp9.c
--- a/libavcodec/cbs_vp9.c
+++ b/libavcodec/cbs_vp9.c
@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@ static int cbs_vp9_split_fragment(CodedBitstreamContext *ctx,
 
         pos = 0;
         for (i = 0; i <= sfi.frames_in_superframe_minus_1; i++) {
-            if (pos + sfi.frame_sizes[i] + index_size > frag->data_size) {
+            if (sfi.frame_sizes[i] > frag->data_size - index_size - pos) {
                 av_log(ctx->log_ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Frame %d too large "
                        "in superframe: %"PRIu32" bytes.\n",
                        i, sfi.frame_sizes[i]);
